1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:03,504
EPISODE 12

2
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,315
Hey!

3
00:00:23,056 --> 00:00:24,625
It's… Yu-na!

4
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:31,098
I'm sorry,
but please let her stay a few days.

5
00:00:31,164 --> 00:00:34,902
What?
Do you think this is a boarding house?

6
00:00:34,968 --> 00:00:37,638
I have my reasons. I'm begging you.

7
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:39,006
Beg all you want,

8
00:00:39,072 --> 00:00:41,875
but we'd need a room
for her to stay in, wouldn't we?

9
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:45,746
Um… There's my room!

10
00:00:45,812 --> 00:00:48,782
I can just sleep with Min-ho.

11
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:52,252
Right! We can just do that.

12
00:00:55,656 --> 00:00:58,792
Then really just for a few days.

13
00:00:58,859 --> 00:00:59,927
Okay, got it.

14
00:00:59,993 --> 00:01:01,895
Thank you so much!

15
00:01:02,863 --> 00:01:04,364
Let's go, Yu-na.

16
00:01:09,436 --> 00:01:11,204
Oh, honestly.

17
00:01:13,874 --> 00:01:15,242
Please come in.

18
00:01:19,446 --> 00:01:21,782
Min-ho must have been in here.

19
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:27,487
Well, um…

20
00:01:27,988 --> 00:01:29,623
please get some rest.

21
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:53,146
Try not to think, and get some sleep.

22
00:01:53,213 --> 00:01:54,815
Tell me if you need anything.

23
00:01:54,881 --> 00:01:55,749
Min-gi.

24
00:01:55,816 --> 00:01:57,651
Let's talk later.

25
00:01:57,718 --> 00:01:59,353
Get some rest.

26
00:01:59,419 --> 00:02:00,587
I'll get going.

27
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:10,097
So that young lady is a celebrity?

28
00:02:10,163 --> 00:02:12,799
No wonder she's so pretty and sexy.

29
00:02:12,866 --> 00:02:14,635
Excuse me?

30
00:02:14,701 --> 00:02:16,670
You're much prettier and sexier.

31
00:02:16,737 --> 00:02:19,573
She's still way too immature.

32
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:23,210
Um, speaking of which,

33
00:02:23,276 --> 00:02:25,078
please don't tell the villagers.

34
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,346
It could cause a stir.

35
00:02:28,915 --> 00:02:30,050
-Will do.
-Okay.

36
00:02:33,854 --> 00:02:36,523
Min-ho, sorry
I couldn't go on the picnic with you.

37
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:39,660
Next time, let's go
somewhere more fun instead, okay?

38
00:02:39,726 --> 00:02:41,395
Okay!

39
00:02:45,432 --> 00:02:46,867
Excuse me, ma'am.

40
00:02:47,601 --> 00:02:49,336
Do you have any leftover food?

41
00:02:49,403 --> 00:02:50,971
Yes, why do you need food?

42
00:02:51,038 --> 00:02:53,440
She must be hungry.
I'd like to get her some.

43
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:56,476
-Then let me get it--
-No, that's okay.

44
00:02:56,543 --> 00:02:57,878
I'll do it myself.

45
00:02:57,944 --> 00:02:59,246
Thank you.

46
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:17,931
Hey, is Yu-na really
involved in that incident…

47
00:03:17,998 --> 00:03:20,434
Stop talking nonsense. That's absurd.

48
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,937
Why get so mad? I was just asking.

49
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:29,342
Hey, knock it off,
and let's go catch grasshoppers.

50
00:03:29,409 --> 00:03:30,510
Excuse me.

51
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:42,089
Yes, hello.

52
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:47,928
Su-yeon!

53
00:03:47,994 --> 00:03:50,297
Jeez, what is it?

54
00:03:50,363 --> 00:03:53,200
I got no sleep from digging all night.

55
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:55,602
Why is that guy here again?

56
00:03:58,438 --> 00:04:00,140
Hello, Su-yeon.

57
00:04:00,207 --> 00:04:01,775
Were you sleeping until now?

58
00:04:01,842 --> 00:04:04,211
Yes, I stayed up planning my painting.

59
00:04:04,277 --> 00:04:05,312
What brings you by?

60
00:04:05,378 --> 00:04:08,048
Someone from Seoul came to see you.

61
00:04:08,115 --> 00:04:11,384
To see me? Who?

62
00:04:11,451 --> 00:04:12,486
Ta-da!

63
00:04:15,856 --> 00:04:17,290
Long time no see.

64
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:20,193
Boss…

65
00:04:21,862 --> 00:04:24,397
What's with your face all day?

66
00:04:24,464 --> 00:04:26,099
Did something happen?

67
00:04:26,166 --> 00:04:30,036
What? No, um… Nothing happened.

68
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:32,606
Hey, where'd you sleep a few days ago?

69
00:04:32,672 --> 00:04:35,375
Who were you with? Got a girlfriend?

70
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:37,377
No, it's nothing like that.

71
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:39,045
Is that so?

72
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:42,215
I'm okay with any woman but Mi-young.

73
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:44,951
Bring anyone home.
Stay out overnight often too.

74
00:04:45,018 --> 00:04:46,286
Got it?

75
00:04:48,321 --> 00:04:49,990
Where am I supposed to sleep?

76
00:04:50,924 --> 00:04:53,593
-You're back, ma'am.
-Yes, I'm back.

77
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:55,629
And who's this lady?

78
00:04:55,695 --> 00:04:59,800
Hello. Su-yeon and I
worked at the same place…

79
00:04:59,866 --> 00:05:02,369
She's my senior from the mural club!

80
00:05:02,435 --> 00:05:05,772
So you came to help with the mural.

81
00:05:05,839 --> 00:05:08,708
Yes, you could say that.

82
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:13,113
So could I stay here for a few days?

83
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:17,150
What? What are you saying right now?

84
00:05:17,217 --> 00:05:19,753
I'd really appreciate it, ma'am.

85
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:23,456
Um, are you married by any chance…

86
00:05:23,523 --> 00:05:25,258
No, not yet.

87
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:27,661
Really? Then please stay with us.

88
00:05:27,727 --> 00:05:30,163
By the way, this is my son.

89
00:05:30,230 --> 00:05:33,266
He's good-looking, kind, and strong.

90
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,735
Mom, what are you talking about again?

91
00:05:35,802 --> 00:05:37,204
Please stop it already.

92
00:05:38,772 --> 00:05:40,774
That little punk, I swear…

93
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:43,009
-Make yourself comfortable.
-Thank you.

94
00:05:43,076 --> 00:05:44,544
Hey, you little punk!

95
00:05:46,913 --> 00:05:49,149
Han-cheol, you should go now.

96
00:05:49,216 --> 00:05:52,586
Pardon? Yes, I will be on my way.

97
00:05:52,652 --> 00:05:54,888
I'm so exhausted.

98
00:05:54,955 --> 00:05:57,591
Let's get inside now, Su-yeon.

99
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:08,101
Look at the sorry state of this room.

100
00:06:09,236 --> 00:06:13,874
Ugh, and what is this awful smell?

101
00:06:16,309 --> 00:06:18,078
What's this?

102
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,085
Don't touch it! No, not that!

103
00:06:26,453 --> 00:06:28,088
What are these?

104
00:06:32,792 --> 00:06:34,861
What? Why so many sweet potatoes?

105
00:06:34,928 --> 00:06:38,331
Jeez, I had my reasons.

106
00:06:38,398 --> 00:06:40,800
Anyway, what's going on?

107
00:06:40,867 --> 00:06:42,202
Why did you come here?

108
00:06:42,269 --> 00:06:47,307
Come on, girl, let's catch our breath.

109
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:51,745
Cut the crap and tell me already.

110
00:06:52,879 --> 00:06:55,448
Five billion won.

111
00:06:58,585 --> 00:07:00,053
What?

112
00:07:00,787 --> 00:07:02,489
Uh… What is that

113
00:07:03,356 --> 00:07:04,524
supposed to mean?

114
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:06,526
I came here knowing everything.

115
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:09,229
So drop the terrible acting.

116
00:07:11,064 --> 00:07:13,767
But how did you know that?

117
00:07:22,075 --> 00:07:23,977
Really no word from Lee Su-yeon?

118
00:07:24,044 --> 00:07:27,781
I… really haven't heard from her.

119
00:07:27,847 --> 00:07:32,118
She even changed her number,
so I really don't know.

120
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:34,287
If by any chance you're lying to us,

121
00:07:35,155 --> 00:07:37,090
you'll die without anyone knowing.

122
00:07:37,924 --> 00:07:40,293
-Understand?
-Yes, I understand.

123
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,594
Hey!

124
00:07:42,929 --> 00:07:45,265
We're having a drink for once.

125
00:07:45,332 --> 00:07:48,168
Enough with the work talk, enough.

126
00:07:49,636 --> 00:07:51,271
Have a drink.

127
00:07:51,338 --> 00:07:52,405
Forget it.

128
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,574
I'll go make a call.

129
00:07:57,110 --> 00:07:59,379
Oh, come on.

130
00:07:59,446 --> 00:08:01,614
What is he, the FBI or the CIA?

131
00:08:01,681 --> 00:08:03,683
He's such a jerk, jeez.

132
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:17,030
So what did Su-yeon do wrong anyway?

133
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:21,534
Are you that curious?

134
00:08:22,302 --> 00:08:24,070
This is a secret.

135
00:08:24,738 --> 00:08:27,073
Don't ever tell that bastard, got it?

136
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:30,910
So, you see, here's what happened.

137
00:08:30,977 --> 00:08:36,216
I think that bitch
pocketed our big boss's money.

138
00:08:38,952 --> 00:08:41,488
Money? How much?

139
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:45,759
Five billion won! All of it in cash.

140
00:08:48,395 --> 00:08:49,629
Five billion won?

141
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:56,236
How can a guy have such a big mouth?
Pathetic bastard.

142
00:08:56,302 --> 00:08:58,938
Anyway, how did you know I was here?

143
00:08:59,005 --> 00:09:00,573
Oh, that?

144
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:04,611
Private detectives
are just like CSI these days.

145
00:09:04,677 --> 00:09:08,381
With just a phone number,
they can track your location and all.

146
00:09:08,448 --> 00:09:10,350
It's mind-blowing.

147
00:09:11,618 --> 00:09:12,619
Don't worry.

148
00:09:12,685 --> 00:09:15,188
I changed my number too before I came.

149
00:09:15,255 --> 00:09:17,123
Those jerks can never find us here.

150
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:22,062
So let's go fifty-fifty. How about it?

151
00:09:24,464 --> 00:09:26,633
I need the money first to go halves!

152
00:09:26,699 --> 00:09:28,968
Hey, are you really going to do this?

153
00:09:29,035 --> 00:09:31,204
I have no money!
I haven't found it yet!

154
00:09:31,271 --> 00:09:32,806
Found it?

155
00:09:32,872 --> 00:09:34,040
What does that mean?

156
00:09:34,107 --> 00:09:37,343
That money's buried somewhere in town.

157
00:09:38,545 --> 00:09:40,613
I've been digging over a month, jeez.

158
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:43,817
No 5 billion or even 50 won.
I just dug up sweet potatoes.

159
00:09:43,883 --> 00:09:46,820
Then you don't even know where it is?

160
00:09:49,756 --> 00:09:52,559
I even closed my bar to come down here…

161
00:09:52,625 --> 00:09:55,929
So drop the false hopes and go back.

162
00:09:55,995 --> 00:09:57,664
Got it?

163
00:09:57,730 --> 00:09:59,265
-We're back.

164
00:09:59,332 --> 00:10:01,000
-Welcome back. Sit.
-Come on in.

165
00:10:01,067 --> 00:10:03,303
You caught a lot of grasshoppers!

166
00:10:03,369 --> 00:10:05,071
Are you hungry? Come on over.

167
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:08,608
Um, how's Yu-na?

168
00:10:09,375 --> 00:10:10,810
No idea. She won't budge.

169
00:10:10,877 --> 00:10:13,113
Do you think she's sleeping? Or eating?

170
00:10:13,179 --> 00:10:15,148
How am I supposed to know that?

171
00:10:15,215 --> 00:10:17,083
You could look after her.

172
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:20,520
What? Come on, am I that woman's maid?

173
00:10:21,187 --> 00:10:23,389
If you care that much, do it yourself.

174
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,191
And so what if she's a star?

175
00:10:25,258 --> 00:10:27,494
What's she doing,
not showing up to eat?

176
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,196
She has no manners at all, none at all!

177
00:10:37,537 --> 00:10:39,606
Yu-na, why… why did you come out?

178
00:10:39,672 --> 00:10:41,641
To get some water…

179
00:10:41,708 --> 00:10:43,877
I… I'll get it for you.

180
00:10:43,943 --> 00:10:45,612
Go back in, go back in.

181
00:11:17,310 --> 00:11:19,045
You've been like this all day?

182
00:11:19,812 --> 00:11:22,582
Get up. Let's go out and eat something.

183
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:26,553
And don't mind what she said.

184
00:11:30,924 --> 00:11:32,659
-Min-gi.
-Yes?

185
00:11:32,725 --> 00:11:34,460
Why aren't you asking anything?

186
00:11:35,228 --> 00:11:38,998
Aren't you curious about what happened?

187
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:45,872
No, I'm not curious.

188
00:11:47,073 --> 00:11:48,408
Because I trust you.

189
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:52,545
Let's go out.

190
00:11:54,847 --> 00:11:56,616
I don't feel like eating.

191
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,085
I'll get some sleep…

192
00:12:15,268 --> 00:12:17,136
Why isn't the young lady coming out?

193
00:12:17,203 --> 00:12:18,705
She says she's not eating.

194
00:12:20,073 --> 00:12:22,208
Why did you have to talk like that?

195
00:12:23,309 --> 00:12:25,311
How could I know she was listening?

196
00:12:26,546 --> 00:12:29,649
-Do you know how to make porridge?
-Why do you ask?

197
00:12:29,716 --> 00:12:31,651
She's so frail, she might collapse.

198
00:12:33,019 --> 00:12:35,188
She's fine! Why porridge and not rice?

199
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:38,258
-Come on, just make her some.
-Gosh, forget it!

200
00:12:38,324 --> 00:12:40,360
That worried? Go cook and serve her!

201
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:43,696
Forget it. I'll do it myself.

202
00:12:43,763 --> 00:12:45,531
Should I do it for you, then?

203
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:48,601
Oh! Um, no, I'll do it myself.

204
00:12:49,869 --> 00:12:51,871
How do I even do this?

205
00:12:58,144 --> 00:13:00,980
Lee Min-gi, get out here! We're late!

206
00:13:01,047 --> 00:13:03,750
I'm coming right now. Quit rushing me.

207
00:13:03,816 --> 00:13:06,486
All the villagers have already left!

208
00:13:06,552 --> 00:13:09,255
Yes, yes, I'm putting on my shoes now.

209
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:13,159
-I'm off.
-Okay, don't worry. Be safe.

210
00:13:14,027 --> 00:13:16,629
Never answer any calls, and eat well.

211
00:13:16,696 --> 00:13:18,798
Don't stay in your room. Get some air.

212
00:13:18,865 --> 00:13:20,133
If you need anything, call me.

213
00:13:20,199 --> 00:13:21,601
Okay.

214
00:13:21,668 --> 00:13:23,636
Hey, Lee Min-gi! I said we're late!

215
00:13:23,703 --> 00:13:25,338
-See you later.
-I'm going.

216
00:13:25,405 --> 00:13:26,339
Take care.

217
00:13:26,406 --> 00:13:29,075
Jeez, get a move on already.

218
00:13:29,142 --> 00:13:30,777
Get some rest.

219
00:13:36,349 --> 00:13:37,917
Hey, hurry it up! Move it!

220
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:40,153
Because of you guys, only we're late!

221
00:13:40,219 --> 00:13:43,289
You'll never load it all at this pace!

222
00:13:43,356 --> 00:13:45,325
Carry two boxes at a time! Two each!

223
00:13:45,391 --> 00:13:47,960
One box is tough! How can I carry two?

224
00:13:48,027 --> 00:13:49,162
Sir, take this box…

225
00:13:49,228 --> 00:13:52,465
These grown men are pathetically weak!

226
00:13:52,532 --> 00:13:54,767
Hey, move aside! Out of the way!

227
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,941
-Strong!
-Village Head's a pro!

228
00:14:02,008 --> 00:14:04,377
Quit yapping and start moving them!

229
00:14:04,444 --> 00:14:05,645
It's not even heavy.

230
00:14:11,384 --> 00:14:13,986
Are you okay? I heard a bone snap.

231
00:14:15,488 --> 00:14:17,357
Oh, no! How do we get through?

232
00:14:17,423 --> 00:14:18,858
I'll go first! Me first!

233
00:14:18,925 --> 00:14:20,259
I said I'm going first!

234
00:14:20,326 --> 00:14:23,329
-Hey! We don't fit! Wait, wait!
-Hey, hold on, wait!

235
00:14:25,164 --> 00:14:26,833
-I'm ripping apart!
-You okay?

236
00:14:29,135 --> 00:14:31,237
-Hold still!
-Hyeok, get me out first!

237
00:14:31,304 --> 00:14:33,172
Stay still, like I said.

238
00:14:33,239 --> 00:14:35,775
-Sir, hurry up!
-Let go of my hair!

239
00:14:35,842 --> 00:14:37,477
-I'm ripping!
-One, two, three!

240
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:40,380
-Careful, be careful!
-One, two, three!

241
00:14:40,446 --> 00:14:41,447
Ouch!

242
00:14:42,849 --> 00:14:44,217
Are you alright?

243
00:14:44,283 --> 00:14:46,285
You guys, I swear!

244
00:14:46,352 --> 00:14:47,954
Are you okay?

245
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:49,222
Lie down, lie down.

246
00:14:50,656 --> 00:14:53,559
Going to the market is hopeless now.

247
00:14:53,626 --> 00:14:56,028
Oh, tell me about it.

248
00:14:56,863 --> 00:14:59,532
Please go run the market in my place.

249
00:14:59,599 --> 00:15:01,334
Gosh, you just make extra work.

250
00:15:02,034 --> 00:15:03,970
Shouldn't you go to the hospital?

251
00:15:04,036 --> 00:15:05,338
Gosh, forget it.

252
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:07,673
A hospital's a waste of money for this.

253
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,542
I'll rest a few hours and be fine.

254
00:15:09,609 --> 00:15:11,244
Don't worry about me.

255
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:13,546
Hurry up and go. Go on, please go.

256
00:15:13,613 --> 00:15:15,648
How can we leave you alone in pain?

257
00:15:15,715 --> 00:15:17,216
Gosh, forget it.

258
00:15:17,283 --> 00:15:19,552
I can take care of myself, so go.

259
00:15:19,619 --> 00:15:21,120
I said hurry up and go!

260
00:15:21,187 --> 00:15:22,422
You can't even get up?

261
00:15:22,488 --> 00:15:25,158
I said don't worry about me, just go!

262
00:15:25,224 --> 00:15:27,360
Man-gu, please take the guys and go.

263
00:15:27,427 --> 00:15:29,095
Min-gi.

264
00:15:30,163 --> 00:15:31,030
What happened?

265
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:34,700
She hurt her back a little.

266
00:15:35,501 --> 00:15:37,437
But who's that young lady?

267
00:15:38,438 --> 00:15:41,474
Sir, that's Yu-na, you know. Yu-na!

268
00:15:41,541 --> 00:15:43,209
Yu-na?

269
00:15:43,276 --> 00:15:44,444
Oh!

270
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:47,246
I'm Man-gu. Nice to meet you.

271
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:49,081
Seriously, sir.

272
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:52,718
-She's Yu-na! Yu-na!
-Right, Yu-na.

273
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:55,188
And I'm Man-gu, too! Man-gu!

274
00:15:55,254 --> 00:15:57,924
-I just introduced myself.
-Yes, right, right.

275
00:15:58,891 --> 00:16:01,394
With that awful hair,
are you a punk or what?

276
00:16:02,328 --> 00:16:03,963
Sir!

277
00:16:05,231 --> 00:16:07,099
Anyway, um…

278
00:16:07,166 --> 00:16:09,836
we must go to the market.
We can't leave her alone.

279
00:16:09,902 --> 00:16:11,504
Um…

280
00:16:11,571 --> 00:16:13,539
I'll stay with her.

281
00:16:13,606 --> 00:16:15,541
-Yu-na, you?
-Yes.

282
00:16:16,709 --> 00:16:19,579
You all seem busy. I'll look after her.

283
00:16:20,613 --> 00:16:22,582
Oh, no, it's okay, it's okay.

284
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:24,884
I'm fine, so please don't mind me.

285
00:16:24,951 --> 00:16:27,386
-I don't need a nurse…
-How are you fine?

286
00:16:27,453 --> 00:16:29,322
You can't even move.

287
00:16:29,388 --> 00:16:31,824
Then look after her, punk young lady.

288
00:16:31,891 --> 00:16:33,860
Yes, don't worry and go on ahead.

289
00:16:34,727 --> 00:16:36,329
We're late. Hurry up, quick!

290
00:16:36,395 --> 00:16:37,463
Look after her.

291
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:39,232
-Look after her.
-See you later.

292
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:43,002
Yu-na, look after her for me.

293
00:16:43,069 --> 00:16:44,337
I'm leaving.

294
00:16:53,913 --> 00:16:55,314
Yes, please come on in.

295
00:16:55,381 --> 00:16:57,350
Yes, please try one before you go.

296
00:16:57,416 --> 00:16:58,851
INDI COUNTY FINE PRODUCE

297
00:16:58,918 --> 00:17:00,219
INDI GINSENG, THE BEST

298
00:17:00,286 --> 00:17:02,321
FRY UP AND EAT SOME PANCAKES

299
00:17:02,388 --> 00:17:03,422
Over here! Here!

300
00:17:03,489 --> 00:17:05,024
MAN-GU'S BEST PINE MUSHROOMS

301
00:17:06,058 --> 00:17:07,293
Come have a taste!

302
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:22,775
EAT SAVORY PANCAKES!
SCALLION, KIMCHI, CHIVE

303
00:17:23,676 --> 00:17:25,645
These are top-quality goods.

304
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,446
Okay, I'll go get the money.

305
00:17:27,513 --> 00:17:29,782
-Yes, come back to Man-gu's stall.
-Okay.

306
00:17:29,849 --> 00:17:32,118
Anyway, I wonder if Yun-hui is okay.

307
00:17:32,184 --> 00:17:35,655
Don't worry, she'll be fine
with that punk young lady by her side.

308
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:37,356
Now I lost count!

309
00:17:37,423 --> 00:17:38,958
Grasshoppers right here!

310
00:17:39,025 --> 00:17:41,928
Sales look pretty good for those punks.

311
00:17:41,994 --> 00:17:43,129
PUFFED BEANS & BUGS!

312
00:17:43,195 --> 00:17:44,497
A TASTE TO DIE FOR!

313
00:17:47,433 --> 00:17:48,534
Here is your order.

314
00:17:48,601 --> 00:17:50,636
-Thank you.
-Thank you, take care!

315
00:17:50,703 --> 00:17:52,705
Healthy and tasty grasshoppers here!

316
00:17:52,772 --> 00:17:54,140
Come on over, everyone!

317
00:17:54,206 --> 00:17:56,342
Come try our grasshoppers! Welcome!

318
00:17:56,409 --> 00:17:58,144
-Welcome!
-May I take your order?

319
00:17:58,210 --> 00:17:59,745
Uh… Grasshoppers, please.

320
00:17:59,812 --> 00:18:01,647
Which flavor would you prefer?

321
00:18:01,714 --> 00:18:03,549
Chili, hot chili grasshopper,

322
00:18:03,616 --> 00:18:05,618
spicy Cheongyang, or Must-hopper.

323
00:18:06,218 --> 00:18:07,320
Must-hopper, please.

324
00:18:07,386 --> 00:18:08,254
Must-hopper.

325
00:18:08,321 --> 00:18:09,889
How would you like it cooked?

326
00:18:09,956 --> 00:18:13,059
We have medium, rare, and well-done.

327
00:18:13,125 --> 00:18:14,760
Yes, well-done, please.

328
00:18:14,827 --> 00:18:17,430
Oh my, you like it fried! Very well.

329
00:18:17,496 --> 00:18:19,398
Must-hopper well-done, takeout!

330
00:18:19,465 --> 00:18:21,834
Must-hopper well-done, thank you mucho!

331
00:18:21,901 --> 00:18:23,135
-Thanks!
-Must-hopper!

332
00:18:23,202 --> 00:18:25,271
Thank you, come again!

333
00:18:25,338 --> 00:18:27,940
Gosh, look at them having a blast.

334
00:18:28,708 --> 00:18:31,110
By the way, I don't see Mr. Han.

335
00:18:31,177 --> 00:18:35,081
I saw him going somewhere
with Sang-eun early this morning.

336
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:48,060
YOON SUK-KYEONG

337
00:19:09,482 --> 00:19:12,551
Honey, I'm here.

338
00:19:13,719 --> 00:19:15,688
It's been a long time.

339
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:21,994
Our daughter, Sang-eun, came with me.

340
00:19:22,061 --> 00:19:26,599
Because of her unworthy father,
she grew up without a mother's warmth.

341
00:19:27,767 --> 00:19:29,335
Our daughter…

342
00:19:31,137 --> 00:19:33,639
I only brought her to meet you now.

343
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:36,709
I'm truly sorry.

344
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:41,013
Sang-eun.

345
00:19:42,381 --> 00:19:45,117
Bow to your mother.

346
00:20:06,939 --> 00:20:09,141
Mom!

347
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,592
DIRECT FARMERS MARKET

348
00:20:27,493 --> 00:20:29,962
Wow, this is a big hit! A big hit!

349
00:20:30,029 --> 00:20:31,063
See? What'd I say?

350
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:32,865
I said it'd be a big hit, right?

351
00:20:32,932 --> 00:20:34,867
Let's ditch cabbage farming early.

352
00:20:34,934 --> 00:20:37,136
-Isn't selling this faster?
-No way.

353
00:20:37,203 --> 00:20:38,504
Bugs and beans are done.

354
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:40,740
We have no ingredients, no ingredients.

355
00:20:42,541 --> 00:20:44,043
YOU LOOK LIKE THIS MUSHROOM?

356
00:20:44,110 --> 00:20:46,112
WHAT? STOP JOKING!

357
00:20:46,178 --> 00:20:47,646
Hey, what's that?

358
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:52,384
Ki-jun, your wife's cheating! Now what?

359
00:20:53,152 --> 00:20:54,787
What? What do you mean? Stop!

360
00:20:54,854 --> 00:20:58,057
How could your wife not cheat
when you treat her so badly?

361
00:20:58,891 --> 00:21:00,526
By the way, who's that guy?

362
00:21:00,593 --> 00:21:02,027
He looks really sharp.

363
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:05,331
He's Chow Yun-fat,
our farmhand from China.

364
00:21:05,397 --> 00:21:07,933
Zhou Runfa? Oh, Chow Yun-fat?

365
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,568
He's as sharp as his name.

366
00:21:10,536 --> 00:21:12,872
I'M NOT JOKING, YOU LOOK ALIKE!
SO IDENTICAL…

367
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:13,806
STOP IT.

368
00:21:13,873 --> 00:21:14,974
-Right?
-Yes.

369
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,977
Plus, speaking the same language,
they got close fast.

370
00:21:18,043 --> 00:21:20,813
Wow, Ki-jun, you should be worried.

371
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:22,615
Me, worried? Please.

372
00:21:22,681 --> 00:21:24,950
Actually, good. She annoyed me anyway.

373
00:21:25,017 --> 00:21:27,119
I hope those two end up together.

374
00:21:28,087 --> 00:21:31,090
Anyway, is Yu-na doing okay?

375
00:21:31,157 --> 00:21:33,626
If you're so worried, go see her now.

376
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:39,365
Why's he being like that to me again?

377
00:21:39,431 --> 00:21:42,368
Stop, stop! Let's count our money.

378
00:21:42,434 --> 00:21:45,237
-Okay.
-One, two, three.

379
00:21:59,018 --> 00:22:01,287
It's so awkward, so awkward.

380
00:22:01,353 --> 00:22:04,623
It's so awkward I'm going crazy.

381
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:09,929
Um… if you're uncomfortable here,

382
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:12,631
you're welcome to go rest in the room.

383
00:22:12,698 --> 00:22:15,868
No, it's okay. I'm fine.

384
00:22:16,869 --> 00:22:18,637
All right.

385
00:22:22,508 --> 00:22:24,176
Ow, that stings!

386
00:22:24,243 --> 00:22:26,645
Darn it, a mosquito bit me.

387
00:22:27,580 --> 00:22:29,181
It's seriously so itchy.

388
00:22:31,317 --> 00:22:34,086
What's wrong? Does something hurt?

389
00:22:34,153 --> 00:22:36,589
Oh, no. It's nothing at all.

390
00:22:36,655 --> 00:22:38,257
Please don't worry.

391
00:22:38,924 --> 00:22:42,895
Jeez, that damn mosquito had to bite
my toe of all places.

392
00:22:45,497 --> 00:22:46,665
What, what's wrong?

393
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:52,504
Oh, you got bitten by a mosquito.

394
00:22:52,571 --> 00:22:54,773
Is it because it's itchy?

395
00:22:54,840 --> 00:22:56,609
No, it's not.

396
00:22:56,675 --> 00:22:58,644
I'm fine, really, I'm fine.

397
00:22:58,711 --> 00:23:00,279
Please don't mind me.

398
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:07,887
It looks really itchy. Um…

399
00:23:09,154 --> 00:23:11,123
shall I scratch it for you?

400
00:23:11,190 --> 00:23:15,227
What? No, goodness, no!
Please don't even say such a thing.

401
00:23:19,131 --> 00:23:22,067
It looks like it really itches.

402
00:23:22,134 --> 00:23:23,669
Let me scratch it gently.

403
00:23:24,336 --> 00:23:26,438
Oh, it's fine, I mean…

404
00:23:27,339 --> 00:23:30,576
then just a little bit, gently,

405
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,913
please…

406
00:23:33,979 --> 00:23:35,314
Okay.

407
00:23:42,488 --> 00:23:45,190
Then I shall commence scratching.

408
00:23:48,594 --> 00:23:49,962
Ouch!

409
00:23:50,496 --> 00:23:52,598
Um, is it because of your nails?

410
00:23:53,332 --> 00:23:54,867
Just a bit gentler, please.

411
00:23:54,934 --> 00:23:56,802
Oh, I'm so sorry.

412
00:23:56,869 --> 00:23:58,704
I meant to scratch it well, but…

413
00:23:58,771 --> 00:24:00,205
It happens.

414
00:24:00,806 --> 00:24:02,508
I shall try scratching again.

415
00:24:02,574 --> 00:24:04,009
Yes, okay.

416
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:11,050
How about like this?

417
00:24:11,917 --> 00:24:13,953
Hold on, wait a second!

418
00:24:14,019 --> 00:24:16,455
A little harder than that.

419
00:24:18,257 --> 00:24:21,627
Then I shall try scratching once more.

420
00:24:24,596 --> 00:24:26,398
How about this?

421
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:28,934
Oh, that pressure is just perfect.

422
00:24:29,001 --> 00:24:31,303
Gosh, that's just right, just right.

423
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:33,405
Jeez, finally, some relief…

424
00:24:34,573 --> 00:24:36,742
I really appreciate it, thank you.

425
00:24:38,210 --> 00:24:39,478
It was nothing.

426
00:24:39,545 --> 00:24:42,247
I should've scratched better.
I've never scratched

427
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:44,083
someone else's mosquito bite.

428
00:24:44,149 --> 00:24:46,051
Oh, not at all.

429
00:24:46,118 --> 00:24:47,953
You're really good at scratching.

430
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:49,388
You're a total pro, a pro.

431
00:24:50,055 --> 00:24:51,557
Thank you.

432
00:25:03,369 --> 00:25:04,903
Good morning.

433
00:25:04,970 --> 00:25:07,673
Morning. Did you sleep well?

434
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:09,675
Yes.

435
00:25:09,742 --> 00:25:11,410
Want some of this?

436
00:25:11,977 --> 00:25:13,812
Oh my, almonds!

437
00:25:13,879 --> 00:25:15,748
Thank you.

438
00:25:19,518 --> 00:25:20,753
They're so moist.

439
00:25:21,887 --> 00:25:24,223
How are these almonds so moist?

440
00:25:24,289 --> 00:25:26,525
Hand me that container.

441
00:25:26,592 --> 00:25:28,327
-This one?
-Yes.

442
00:25:30,129 --> 00:25:31,096
They're tasty.

443
00:25:34,299 --> 00:25:36,702
This weather is so nice.

444
00:25:46,478 --> 00:25:49,081
Why is this dripping? What a mess.

445
00:25:53,052 --> 00:25:54,319
Ow, that's hot!

446
00:25:54,386 --> 00:25:55,654
Ow, that's hot!

447
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:58,957
Jeez, be careful! Get it together!

448
00:26:00,526 --> 00:26:02,094
-Ki-jun.
-What?

449
00:26:02,161 --> 00:26:03,695
Am I really that bad?

450
00:26:03,762 --> 00:26:05,931
Jeez, do you even have to…

451
00:26:06,732 --> 00:26:07,599
But why?

452
00:26:07,666 --> 00:26:09,435
Su-yeon says she'd never date me.

453
00:26:09,501 --> 00:26:11,036
She told me to give up now.

454
00:26:11,103 --> 00:26:12,871
Why? What's the reason?

455
00:26:12,938 --> 00:26:15,541
I don't know. She can't tell me why,

456
00:26:15,607 --> 00:26:18,310
and she says telling me won't fix it.

457
00:26:18,377 --> 00:26:19,411
What could it be?

458
00:26:23,782 --> 00:26:26,051
Maybe she likes women instead of men?

459
00:26:28,320 --> 00:26:30,622
Does that make any sense? You crazy…

460
00:26:31,990 --> 00:26:34,259
I'm the crazy one for asking you.

461
00:26:34,326 --> 00:26:35,861
I'm really such an idiot.

462
00:26:35,928 --> 00:26:37,429
No need to get mad, jeez.

463
00:26:38,997 --> 00:26:40,399
It's all burned!

464
00:26:40,466 --> 00:26:42,835
Foreign language dialogue.

465
00:26:42,901 --> 00:26:46,472
Foreign language dialogue.

466
00:26:49,641 --> 00:26:51,577
IS THAT THE MAN YOU LIKE?

467
00:26:51,643 --> 00:26:52,978
YES.

468
00:26:53,045 --> 00:26:55,080
HE'S MANLY AND HANDSOME.

469
00:26:55,147 --> 00:26:57,916
STOP IT, YOU'RE EMBARRASSING ME.

470
00:26:59,651 --> 00:27:02,054
They are just thrilled to death.

471
00:27:02,121 --> 00:27:03,288
Good luck to you two.

472
00:27:03,355 --> 00:27:05,991
I only fell for
her pretty face and nice figure.

473
00:27:06,058 --> 00:27:08,293
I don't actually like her! Not at all!

474
00:27:17,503 --> 00:27:19,771
-Excuse me, Ki-jun?
-What is it?

475
00:27:19,838 --> 00:27:22,207
Can you pick up
the packing string behind you?

476
00:27:36,421 --> 00:27:38,257
Here, take it.

477
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:48,400
Why are you smiling?

478
00:27:53,639 --> 00:27:54,773
So what if I smile?

479
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:56,575
Can't I smile if I want to?

480
00:28:10,956 --> 00:28:12,024
Hey, you punk!

481
00:28:12,090 --> 00:28:14,293
Why do you keep bugging the poor thing?

482
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:15,727
What did I do?

483
00:28:15,794 --> 00:28:19,131
That rotten kid! My throat is parched!

484
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:21,900
Hey, go buy some drinks over there.

485
00:28:21,967 --> 00:28:23,368
Why make me do that?

486
00:28:23,435 --> 00:28:27,172
Buy them when I say, you little brat!

487
00:28:27,239 --> 00:28:28,774
All right.

488
00:28:33,779 --> 00:28:36,248
-Here you go.
-Right, good job.

489
00:28:36,315 --> 00:28:38,784
Have a drink while you work, everyone.

490
00:28:38,850 --> 00:28:41,086
-Yes, hand some out.
-Here, have a drink.

491
00:28:43,021 --> 00:28:45,324
Excuse me, Ki-jun?

492
00:28:45,390 --> 00:28:47,326
Please give me just two drinks.

493
00:28:48,627 --> 00:28:50,629
Go get them yourself. Do it yourself.

494
00:28:50,696 --> 00:28:53,131
Yes, I understand.

495
00:28:56,134 --> 00:28:57,669
Wait, no!

496
00:28:59,538 --> 00:29:01,873
I'll get them for you. Hold on.

497
00:29:12,150 --> 00:29:13,652
Here you are.

498
00:29:13,719 --> 00:29:17,022
Go on, drink up while they're cold.

499
00:29:28,834 --> 00:29:31,536
Ki-jun?

500
00:29:34,139 --> 00:29:35,574
SHINSEONG CIDER

501
00:29:38,644 --> 00:29:40,779
I changed my mind. Get it yourself.

502
00:29:42,347 --> 00:29:45,350
Gosh, that's why you should be nicer.

503
00:29:45,417 --> 00:29:47,452
Why do you keep picking on Hwa-ran?

504
00:29:49,321 --> 00:29:51,089
What did I do?

505
00:30:18,083 --> 00:30:21,787
Um… you can go back to your room now.

506
00:30:22,287 --> 00:30:25,057
I'll call if I really need anything.

507
00:30:25,724 --> 00:30:27,559
No, I'm really fine.

508
00:30:27,626 --> 00:30:30,062
Oh, I'm really… fine too.

509
00:30:31,430 --> 00:30:34,132
I'm getting a little sleepy now.

510
00:30:34,199 --> 00:30:38,003
The thing is, I'm much more
sensitive than you'd think.

511
00:30:38,070 --> 00:30:41,006
I can't sleep with someone next to me.

512
00:30:41,073 --> 00:30:42,274
Is that so?

513
00:30:45,310 --> 00:30:47,546
I understand. I'll head back then.

514
00:30:47,612 --> 00:30:50,015
-Yes, okay.
-Call me if you need anything.

515
00:30:50,082 --> 00:30:51,483
Yes, get some rest.

516
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:54,353
Go ahead.

517
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:02,260
I have to pee so badly I almost died.

518
00:31:02,327 --> 00:31:04,363
Why stay here when I told her to go?

519
00:31:04,429 --> 00:31:06,264
She made me so uncomfortable.

520
00:31:06,331 --> 00:31:07,466
Bathroom, bathroom!

521
00:31:33,458 --> 00:31:36,495
Okay, just a little bit farther.

522
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:38,163
I'm almost there now.

523
00:31:38,230 --> 00:31:40,332
Just a little more.

524
00:31:40,399 --> 00:31:41,733
Just a little more.

525
00:31:42,534 --> 00:31:44,035
Hang in there!

526
00:32:10,862 --> 00:32:13,432
Okay, I made it, I made it.

527
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:17,436
This is really the final spurt.

528
00:32:21,273 --> 00:32:24,576
Oh no, this is killing me! Mommy!

529
00:32:26,645 --> 00:32:29,581
What's wrong? Did something happen?

530
00:32:29,648 --> 00:32:32,517
Oh, no, it's nothing. Nothing at all.

531
00:32:32,584 --> 00:32:34,486
Need the bathroom? Can I help you?

532
00:32:34,553 --> 00:32:37,422
What? Gosh, no, not at all!

533
00:32:38,890 --> 00:32:39,891
You're really okay?

534
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:42,594
Oh, of course. I'm fine, I'm fine.

535
00:32:42,661 --> 00:32:45,464
Then call me if you need anything.

536
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:47,666
-Excuse me…
-Yes?

537
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,002
I'm really sorry.

538
00:32:51,069 --> 00:32:52,571
Could you help me…

539
00:32:53,705 --> 00:32:56,208
just a little bit?

540
00:32:56,274 --> 00:32:58,910
I'm coming in then.

541
00:33:02,881 --> 00:33:04,883
Are you okay?

542
00:33:08,753 --> 00:33:12,524
Um… I'm really sorry.

543
00:33:12,591 --> 00:33:14,226
Well…

544
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:19,164
could you help me onto the toilet

545
00:33:19,231 --> 00:33:21,333
and sit me down gently?

546
00:33:22,601 --> 00:33:24,870
Slowly… slowly.

547
00:33:28,206 --> 00:33:29,875
Nice and slow.

548
00:33:48,326 --> 00:33:52,264
Um… would you be able
to pull your pants down?

549
00:33:52,330 --> 00:33:55,333
Oh, of course!
I should pull my pants down myself.

550
00:33:56,601 --> 00:33:57,869
-I'll leave then.
-Okay.

551
00:34:03,742 --> 00:34:07,646
Um, I'm really sorry, but…

552
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:11,850
could you pull my pants down too?

553
00:34:11,917 --> 00:34:13,652
What?

554
00:34:21,426 --> 00:34:25,797
Um, I'm really sorry, but…

555
00:34:27,332 --> 00:34:31,403
could you turn your head a little?

556
00:34:31,469 --> 00:34:33,972
Oh, um, I'm sorry.

557
00:34:34,039 --> 00:34:36,441
I'm really sorry.

558
00:34:38,476 --> 00:34:40,111
Be careful here.

559
00:34:46,985 --> 00:34:48,954
-Take it slow.
-Okay.

560
00:34:49,020 --> 00:34:50,555
Ugh, this thing…

561
00:34:50,622 --> 00:34:53,458
sure does hurt quite a bit.

562
00:34:53,525 --> 00:34:55,594
-Let's go down.
-Wait, wait.

563
00:34:56,761 --> 00:34:58,597
Ow!

564
00:35:11,476 --> 00:35:12,444
Are you okay?

565
00:35:12,510 --> 00:35:15,213
Yes, I'm fine.

566
00:35:16,081 --> 00:35:18,383
Do you need anything else?

567
00:35:19,351 --> 00:35:20,919
No, I don't.

568
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:23,054
Not at all.

569
00:35:23,688 --> 00:35:25,323
Nothing.

570
00:35:27,525 --> 00:35:29,027
Go on and get some rest.

571
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:32,063
Then I shall take my leave.

572
00:35:43,642 --> 00:35:46,244
I made some food
with what was in the fridge.

573
00:35:48,179 --> 00:35:50,882
But will you be able to eat?

574
00:35:50,949 --> 00:35:53,418
Of course, I should eat on my own.

575
00:35:53,485 --> 00:35:55,587
Obviously, I can do that.

576
00:35:59,424 --> 00:36:00,892
This isn't going to work.

577
00:36:00,959 --> 00:36:02,594
I'll just feed you.

578
00:36:02,661 --> 00:36:03,762
Take it slow.

579
00:36:04,529 --> 00:36:06,164
Take it slow.

580
00:36:12,437 --> 00:36:15,507
-Ah.

581
00:36:24,349 --> 00:36:27,318
-Ah.

582
00:36:30,488 --> 00:36:33,091
How is it? Is it to your taste?

583
00:36:33,158 --> 00:36:35,794
Yes, it's really delicious.

584
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:38,697
Wow, you're actually a great cook.

585
00:36:39,364 --> 00:36:42,901
I thought you lived a pampered life,
so this is a real surprise.

586
00:36:43,735 --> 00:36:46,805
Actually, I've lived alone
since I was 14.

587
00:36:47,572 --> 00:36:49,507
Since you were 14?

588
00:36:49,574 --> 00:36:51,743
You mean since seventh grade?

589
00:36:51,810 --> 00:36:53,044
Why?

590
00:36:53,912 --> 00:36:56,381
I lived in a dorm as a trainee then.

591
00:36:57,015 --> 00:37:00,151
I'm great at cooking,
cleaning, and doing laundry.

592
00:37:00,218 --> 00:37:02,721
And I can even fix most appliances.

593
00:37:04,689 --> 00:37:08,493
Eat this and get some sleep.
That'll help you recover faster.

594
00:37:09,494 --> 00:37:11,529
-Ah.

595
00:37:19,003 --> 00:37:20,672
Please eat plenty!

596
00:37:21,973 --> 00:37:24,375
You all worked hard today, everyone.

597
00:37:24,442 --> 00:37:26,111
Eat up, everyone.

598
00:37:26,945 --> 00:37:28,580
Today, this is all on us!

599
00:37:28,646 --> 00:37:30,415
-Please eat plenty!
-Really?

600
00:37:30,482 --> 00:37:32,584
Business went well today, didn't it?

601
00:37:32,650 --> 00:37:34,385
We totally hit the jackpot!

602
00:37:34,452 --> 00:37:36,888
Not a single grasshopper leg was left!

603
00:37:36,955 --> 00:37:39,958
Never thought I'd live to get
a free meal from you guys.

604
00:37:40,024 --> 00:37:41,726
I never knew, never, never!

605
00:37:41,793 --> 00:37:46,097
Come on, eat up quickly
so we can head back before dark.

606
00:37:46,164 --> 00:37:48,600
Chow Yun-fat and Hwa-ran, eat up.

607
00:37:49,234 --> 00:37:50,568
IS IT GOOD?

608
00:37:50,635 --> 00:37:51,669
YES, IT'S GOOD.

609
00:37:51,736 --> 00:37:53,037
EAT PLENTY.

610
00:38:11,222 --> 00:38:13,925
-What's this?
-What do you mean, you crazy bastard!

611
00:38:13,992 --> 00:38:15,827
What do you think you're doing?

612
00:38:20,064 --> 00:38:21,366
Did I really do this?

613
00:38:21,432 --> 00:38:23,802
I've never seen such a crazy bastard!

614
00:38:23,868 --> 00:38:27,138
What on earth have you been doing
to this poor girl?

615
00:38:27,205 --> 00:38:30,108
Are you human or the devil, punk?

616
00:38:30,175 --> 00:38:33,278
-Even the devil wouldn't do this.
-No, I didn't mean it.

617
00:38:33,344 --> 00:38:35,180
I thought I was imagining it.

618
00:38:35,246 --> 00:38:37,916
Imagining it, my foot! You bastard!

619
00:38:37,982 --> 00:38:40,418
Hwa-ran, that's not it.
I'm sorry-- Ow!

620
00:38:40,485 --> 00:38:42,287
Chow Yun-fat, that's not it!

621
00:38:42,353 --> 00:38:45,223
Even Min-gi wouldn't do that, punk.

622
00:38:45,290 --> 00:38:47,125
Right! I'd never… Wait, damn it!

623
00:38:49,093 --> 00:38:51,095
I think someone's inside me.

624
00:38:51,162 --> 00:38:52,897
I think someone's inside me.

625
00:38:54,732 --> 00:38:56,334
Come on, do some work.

626
00:38:56,401 --> 00:38:58,336
-What are you doing?
-I am working!

627
00:38:58,403 --> 00:38:59,838
Aren't you working, girl?

628
00:38:59,904 --> 00:39:01,306
-Over here.
-Put it there.

629
00:39:01,372 --> 00:39:03,208
All right, everyone!

630
00:39:03,274 --> 00:39:05,009
We have a market after-party!

631
00:39:05,076 --> 00:39:07,345
Let's all have makgeolli before we go.

632
00:39:07,412 --> 00:39:08,580
Oh, sounds great!

633
00:39:08,646 --> 00:39:11,716
I'll head out first.
My dad and Eun-u are waiting.

634
00:39:11,783 --> 00:39:14,419
You said a caregiver is with him.

635
00:39:14,485 --> 00:39:18,156
On a day like today, we should drink
and catch up on old times.

636
00:39:18,990 --> 00:39:19,858
Okay.

637
00:39:19,924 --> 00:39:21,926
I'm tired, so I'll head home first.

638
00:39:21,993 --> 00:39:26,130
Are you dying or something?
Why are you acting so unlike yourself?

639
00:39:26,197 --> 00:39:28,766
You can't turn down a drink. Come on.

640
00:39:28,833 --> 00:39:30,535
-Come on, punk.
-Let's go in too.

641
00:39:30,602 --> 00:39:31,703
Come on, hurry up.

642
00:39:32,503 --> 00:39:33,371
Hurry on over.

643
00:39:34,606 --> 00:39:36,407
I'm heading home for Yu-na too.

644
00:39:37,242 --> 00:39:39,544
Sorry, I have somewhere to go too.

645
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:41,379
I'm tired too.

646
00:39:41,446 --> 00:39:43,014
I'll have a drink first.

647
00:39:49,153 --> 00:39:51,589
My battery's dead.

648
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:55,159
Head back tomorrow, got it?

649
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:59,097
I told you, I closed up shop and came.

650
00:39:59,931 --> 00:40:02,734
I have nowhere to go, girl.

651
00:40:04,669 --> 00:40:06,204
Su-yeon.

652
00:40:06,271 --> 00:40:09,073
I can never give up on you.

653
00:40:09,140 --> 00:40:11,509
No, I will never give up on you.

654
00:40:11,576 --> 00:40:15,079
So you give up on pushing me away.

655
00:40:15,146 --> 00:40:16,214
And take this.

656
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:18,516
It's dried sweet potato.

657
00:40:18,583 --> 00:40:19,984
I heard it lasts so long.

658
00:40:20,051 --> 00:40:24,088
So you don't have to go steal
sweet potatoes at night anymore.

659
00:40:24,722 --> 00:40:26,557
I love you.

660
00:40:26,624 --> 00:40:27,959
I'll be going now.

661
00:40:28,793 --> 00:40:31,062
Wow, my charisma is awesome!

662
00:40:32,730 --> 00:40:36,067
Should I do it like this?

663
00:40:36,134 --> 00:40:38,269
Honestly, I'm kind of nervous.

664
00:40:42,206 --> 00:40:43,474
Let's go.

665
00:40:46,844 --> 00:40:49,047
Are you really going to be like this?

666
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:50,982
Why are you exhausting me like this?

667
00:40:51,049 --> 00:40:53,651
Are you that unhappy that I came?

668
00:40:53,718 --> 00:40:55,954
Is that all we were to each other?

669
00:40:56,020 --> 00:40:57,689
Think about it.

670
00:40:57,755 --> 00:40:59,590
You and I were so good together.

671
00:40:59,657 --> 00:41:04,062
We met up every single day,
ate together, and went out.

672
00:41:04,128 --> 00:41:06,230
We were always together.

673
00:41:07,865 --> 00:41:09,968
I like you too. I really mean it.

674
00:41:10,034 --> 00:41:12,170
But this isn't right.

675
00:41:12,236 --> 00:41:13,871
This'll be harder on us both.

676
00:41:13,938 --> 00:41:17,075
So go back right away tomorrow, okay?

677
00:41:17,141 --> 00:41:19,243
No, I can't go.

678
00:41:19,844 --> 00:41:22,313
I'm not going. I'll stay by your side.

679
00:41:22,380 --> 00:41:24,148
Seriously, why are you doing this?

680
00:41:24,215 --> 00:41:26,584
If people here find out about our past,

681
00:41:26,651 --> 00:41:28,553
we'll both get kicked out.

682
00:41:28,619 --> 00:41:32,190
Did we commit a crime or something?

683
00:41:32,957 --> 00:41:35,026
Conservative people here won't get it.

684
00:41:35,093 --> 00:41:37,161
So please stop making it hard on me.

685
00:41:37,228 --> 00:41:39,530
Just leave already.

686
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:44,535
Su-yeon, I'm begging you like this.

687
00:41:44,602 --> 00:41:49,407
For old times' sake,
just let me stay by your side.

688
00:41:57,715 --> 00:42:01,152
Did you hear a noise just now?

689
00:42:08,626 --> 00:42:09,827
Nobody's out here.

690
00:42:12,797 --> 00:42:15,533
Huh? What's this?

691
00:42:16,067 --> 00:42:17,735
What is it?

692
00:42:19,570 --> 00:42:21,773
It looks like dried sweet potato.

693
00:42:21,839 --> 00:42:25,376
Sweet potato? Why is this here?

694
00:42:25,443 --> 00:42:29,514
Never mind that. It's late,
so let's just go to sleep, Su-yeon.

695
00:42:30,181 --> 00:42:34,852
Let's get cozy, just the two of us,
and cuddle up nice and tight in bed.

696
00:42:43,061 --> 00:42:46,297
No, that can't be true.

697
00:42:50,334 --> 00:42:53,371
Gosh, I must've dozed off.

698
00:42:54,305 --> 00:42:56,174
What time is it now?

699
00:42:57,308 --> 00:42:59,243
Nine o'clock?

700
00:42:59,310 --> 00:43:02,680
Oh my, how many hours did I sleep?

701
00:43:02,747 --> 00:43:05,116
I haven't even fed Min-ho. This is bad.

702
00:43:11,322 --> 00:43:12,990
When did you get here?

703
00:43:13,057 --> 00:43:15,860
I just got here. How's your back?

704
00:43:15,927 --> 00:43:18,129
I got some rest, so it's much better.

705
00:43:18,196 --> 00:43:19,931
Min-ho, are you hungry?

706
00:43:19,997 --> 00:43:21,799
I'm sorry. I'll get you food now.

707
00:43:21,866 --> 00:43:25,002
No, I already ate.

708
00:43:26,404 --> 00:43:29,006
A pretty lady made it for me.

709
00:43:29,073 --> 00:43:30,842
A pretty lady?

710
00:43:31,476 --> 00:43:33,311
Please have some fruit.

711
00:43:33,878 --> 00:43:34,912
Um, Yu-na…

712
00:43:34,979 --> 00:43:39,917
I heard this young lady fed Min-ho
and helped him with his homework.

713
00:43:39,984 --> 00:43:44,489
Plus, she even did all the dishes
and cleaned the whole house spotless.

714
00:43:44,555 --> 00:43:46,190
Is that so?

715
00:43:47,558 --> 00:43:48,726
Thank you.

716
00:43:49,427 --> 00:43:51,629
It was nothing, really.

717
00:43:51,696 --> 00:43:53,431
That feels so refreshing.

718
00:43:53,498 --> 00:43:55,433
-Uncle, you're here?
-Yes.

719
00:43:55,500 --> 00:43:59,670
What? You came straight back
without having an after-party?

720
00:43:59,737 --> 00:44:00,805
I was just tired.

721
00:44:02,540 --> 00:44:04,909
Yu-na, everything okay? Did you eat?

722
00:44:04,976 --> 00:44:06,244
Yes, I ate.

723
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:08,246
So, did the sales go well?

724
00:44:08,312 --> 00:44:11,682
Of course. We completely sold out.

725
00:44:12,683 --> 00:44:14,719
Anyway, I'm glad it went well.

726
00:44:14,785 --> 00:44:16,854
What's that in your hand?

727
00:44:17,889 --> 00:44:21,459
This? Since I was in Seoul,
I bought a few things Yu-na needed.

728
00:44:21,526 --> 00:44:23,661
Yu-na came in a hurry with nothing.

729
00:44:24,428 --> 00:44:25,396
Here you go.

730
00:44:25,463 --> 00:44:26,731
Thanks.

731
00:44:34,172 --> 00:44:35,673
Here.

732
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:37,341
What is this?

733
00:44:37,408 --> 00:44:40,044
A pain patch? One measly pain patch?

734
00:44:40,111 --> 00:44:42,713
I almost didn't even
buy you this, you know.

735
00:44:42,780 --> 00:44:44,982
Lower your expectations.

736
00:44:49,720 --> 00:44:51,589
Are you sulking?

737
00:44:55,660 --> 00:44:56,827
Here you go.

738
00:44:56,894 --> 00:44:58,496
What is this?

739
00:45:00,398 --> 00:45:01,732
Is it cosmetics?

740
00:45:01,799 --> 00:45:04,268
They say this is great for anti-aging.

741
00:45:04,335 --> 00:45:06,871
You have crinkly wrinkles
here under your eyes.

742
00:45:06,938 --> 00:45:08,439
Start putting it on early.

743
00:45:08,506 --> 00:45:11,209
Who knows?
Some blind guy might fall for you.

744
00:45:11,275 --> 00:45:12,877
Why, you little punk!

745
00:45:12,944 --> 00:45:14,278
I'm out of here!

746
00:45:23,187 --> 00:45:26,624
All right, everyone, great work today!

747
00:45:26,691 --> 00:45:29,260
This is all on me, Man-gu!

748
00:45:29,327 --> 00:45:31,596
Have a nice cold drink!

749
00:45:31,662 --> 00:45:33,097
Now, cheers!

750
00:45:33,164 --> 00:45:34,966
Cheers!

751
00:45:35,032 --> 00:45:36,934
Great work today, everyone.

752
00:45:37,001 --> 00:45:38,636
It went really, really well.

753
00:45:41,272 --> 00:45:43,274
But why are you two so awkward today?

754
00:45:43,341 --> 00:45:44,208
Anything wrong?

755
00:45:44,275 --> 00:45:45,610
-No!

756
00:45:45,676 --> 00:45:47,345
-Nothing's wrong.
-Unbelievable.

757
00:45:47,411 --> 00:45:50,014
Then just say no. Why yell like that?

758
00:45:55,286 --> 00:45:56,354
And that punk…

759
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:59,257
why is a young kid
guzzling booze like that?

760
00:45:59,323 --> 00:46:01,592
Hey, punk! What's wrong with you?

761
00:46:01,659 --> 00:46:04,662
He snapped at Hwa-ran,
and now it's bothering him.

762
00:46:04,729 --> 00:46:06,297
That's not true at all.

763
00:46:06,364 --> 00:46:07,898
Why would I care about her?

764
00:46:07,965 --> 00:46:10,134
If not, fine. How dare you snap at me?

765
00:46:10,201 --> 00:46:12,270
Because you're making me mad, lady!

766
00:46:12,336 --> 00:46:14,272
That… What an ill-mannered punk!

767
00:46:17,008 --> 00:46:18,242
That little bastard…

768
00:46:19,343 --> 00:46:21,112
Just leave him be.

769
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:23,981
Um, by the way…

770
00:46:24,048 --> 00:46:27,018
I called In-gi earlier,
so why isn't he here yet?

771
00:46:27,084 --> 00:46:30,588
Why invite that guy to ruin the mood?

772
00:46:30,655 --> 00:46:33,557
Mom, why do you hate In-gi so much?

773
00:46:33,624 --> 00:46:36,861
He puts me in a bad mood,
and he has a prickly temper.

774
00:46:36,927 --> 00:46:39,497
Anyway, I just can't warm up to him.

775
00:46:41,198 --> 00:46:43,534
-Hello.
-Oh?

776
00:46:43,601 --> 00:46:45,736
In-gi, my friend, you're here!

777
00:46:45,803 --> 00:46:49,240
We were having a drink,
and I kept thinking of you.

778
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:51,309
That's why I called you!

779
00:46:53,311 --> 00:46:54,178
Thank you.

780
00:46:54,245 --> 00:46:56,314
No need for thanks between you and me.

781
00:46:56,380 --> 00:46:57,782
In-gi, right here…

782
00:46:59,050 --> 00:47:00,217
Huh?

783
00:47:01,319 --> 00:47:02,853
-Huh?
-What's the matter?

784
00:47:07,191 --> 00:47:10,061
What's going on? Wait, he's talking?

785
00:47:10,127 --> 00:47:12,663
My dad can talk now.

786
00:47:13,164 --> 00:47:14,498
His aphasia is cured!

787
00:47:17,301 --> 00:47:21,138
Really? In-gi, that's such a relief.

788
00:47:21,205 --> 00:47:22,973
Thank you.

789
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:26,911
Um…

790
00:47:26,977 --> 00:47:29,947
I have been so indebted to you all,

791
00:47:30,715 --> 00:47:32,316
and I was sorry for so much,

792
00:47:32,383 --> 00:47:35,986
yet I could never once say thank you.

793
00:47:37,088 --> 00:47:40,024
I would like to take this opportunity
to say it today.

794
00:47:41,392 --> 00:47:44,795
I am truly grateful, and I thank you.

795
00:47:44,862 --> 00:47:48,265
I ask for your continued kindness.

796
00:47:51,001 --> 00:47:55,873
What a blessing for our village!
What a blessing!

797
00:47:55,940 --> 00:48:00,077
All right, to celebrate In-gi
getting his voice back,

798
00:48:00,144 --> 00:48:01,412
let's make a toast.

799
00:48:01,479 --> 00:48:03,848
In-gi, have a seat. Sit down.

800
00:48:03,914 --> 00:48:08,252
Okay, when I say one, two, three,
we all say cheers!

801
00:48:08,319 --> 00:48:11,122
One, two, three, cheers!

802
00:48:11,188 --> 00:48:13,657
-Cheers.
-Congratulations, my friend!

803
00:48:13,724 --> 00:48:14,992
My, that's amazing.

804
00:48:20,698 --> 00:48:22,666
Please accept a drink, Madam Kim.

805
00:48:22,733 --> 00:48:24,835
Pardon? Madam?

806
00:48:24,902 --> 00:48:27,037
Oh, yes, of course.

807
00:48:27,104 --> 00:48:30,174
You must have felt so frustrated
because of me, right?

808
00:48:30,241 --> 00:48:31,175
I apologize.

809
00:48:31,242 --> 00:48:34,278
Not at all, it's quite all right.

810
00:48:40,785 --> 00:48:43,354
Talking makes him look like a new man.

811
00:48:43,421 --> 00:48:47,291
His voice is pure honey. Golden pipes!

812
00:48:49,160 --> 00:48:51,028
Why care about a woman like her?

813
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:53,431
An illegal immigrant, at that.

814
00:48:54,098 --> 00:48:56,267
THE MARKET WAS TOUGH TODAY, RIGHT?

815
00:48:56,333 --> 00:48:58,769
YES, A LITTLE.

816
00:48:58,836 --> 00:49:02,106
WHAT'S THAT GUY'S DEAL?
WHY DOES HE TREAT YOU LIKE THAT?

817
00:49:05,476 --> 00:49:07,611
ARE YOU OKAY?

818
00:49:07,678 --> 00:49:09,513
I'M FINE.

819
00:49:11,148 --> 00:49:15,786
BUT I THINK I'LL GIVE UP ON HIM NOW…

820
00:49:15,853 --> 00:49:19,190
I THINK I FORGOT MY PLACE,
BEING AN ILLEGAL IMMIGRANT…

821
00:49:19,256 --> 00:49:24,195
RIGHT, IT MIGHT BE BETTER TO STOP
BEFORE YOU GET HURT EVEN MORE.

822
00:49:24,261 --> 00:49:27,965
HWA-RAN, CHEER UP! I'M HERE FOR YOU…

823
00:49:28,799 --> 00:49:30,701
Foreign dialogue

824
00:49:34,772 --> 00:49:36,373
Ki-jun…

825
00:49:41,178 --> 00:49:43,814
Why are you doing this?
Let go of my hand!

826
00:49:46,650 --> 00:49:49,820
Do you not hear me? Let go right now!

827
00:49:52,356 --> 00:49:54,492
Why on earth are you doing this to me?

828
00:49:54,558 --> 00:49:57,761
What did I do wrong to you
for you to treat me like this?

829
00:49:57,828 --> 00:49:59,129
Don't smile at everyone.

830
00:50:01,232 --> 00:50:02,566
-Pardon?
-It bothers me.

831
00:50:02,633 --> 00:50:04,668
I said don't smile at just anyone.

832
00:50:04,735 --> 00:50:06,670
Don't even look at other men.

833
00:50:06,737 --> 00:50:09,173
Don't talk to them or smile at them!

834
00:50:13,744 --> 00:50:15,813
Oh, this is driving me crazy.

835
00:50:16,480 --> 00:50:18,616
I can't keep avoiding her forever.

836
00:50:18,682 --> 00:50:21,919
But is Mi-young still into me too?

837
00:50:21,986 --> 00:50:23,254
She must be, right?

838
00:50:23,320 --> 00:50:26,790
She wouldn't have done that otherwise.

839
00:50:44,041 --> 00:50:48,245
Gosh, it's really cold out, isn't it?

840
00:50:48,913 --> 00:50:51,682
Oh, uh, right, it is.

841
00:50:51,749 --> 00:50:56,287
It's so dark since it's night, right?

842
00:50:57,354 --> 00:51:00,324
Um, Sang-deuk.

843
00:51:00,391 --> 00:51:01,792
Yes?

844
00:51:02,560 --> 00:51:04,862
About what happened a few days ago.

845
00:51:04,929 --> 00:51:07,598
Yes, uh… that.

846
00:51:08,866 --> 00:51:11,702
I think I was too drunk
and made a mistake.

847
00:51:13,704 --> 00:51:14,572
A mistake?

848
00:51:15,873 --> 00:51:18,008
Right, of course it was a mistake.

849
00:51:18,075 --> 00:51:20,377
I regretted it so much too.

850
00:51:21,478 --> 00:51:24,248
So let's pretend it never happened.

851
00:51:24,315 --> 00:51:28,852
Uh… Right, of course
we should pretend it never happened.

852
00:51:28,919 --> 00:51:31,622
Gosh, that darn alcohol's the problem.

853
00:51:31,689 --> 00:51:35,025
We're still close,
like brother and sister, right?

854
00:51:35,092 --> 00:51:38,729
Of course! We're close,
like brother and sister.

855
00:51:38,796 --> 00:51:42,800
Then as brother and sister,
should we go in and finish our drinks?

856
00:51:43,567 --> 00:51:44,535
Should we?

857
00:51:58,582 --> 00:52:00,751
Did I just snore?

858
00:52:00,818 --> 00:52:02,586
Wait, the time…

859
00:52:03,921 --> 00:52:05,889
It's already this late…

860
00:52:05,956 --> 00:52:07,758
Hey, let's all go home now.

861
00:52:07,825 --> 00:52:09,827
You go on ahead.

862
00:52:09,893 --> 00:52:12,830
We're close, like brother and sister,

863
00:52:12,896 --> 00:52:15,032
so we'll have one more drink and go.

864
00:52:17,534 --> 00:52:19,770
Just the two of you this late at night?

865
00:52:19,837 --> 00:52:21,639
Why?

866
00:52:21,705 --> 00:52:25,643
We're close, like brother and sister,
so what's the big deal?

867
00:52:26,977 --> 00:52:30,180
If his mom catches you,
she'll tear you to pieces.

868
00:52:30,247 --> 00:52:32,082
It's fine.

869
00:52:32,149 --> 00:52:35,252
My mom went to a prayer retreat today,

870
00:52:35,319 --> 00:52:37,421
so she won't be back until near dawn.

871
00:52:37,488 --> 00:52:40,858
Plus, we're like brother and sister,

872
00:52:40,924 --> 00:52:42,926
so what's wrong with having a drink?

873
00:52:43,861 --> 00:52:45,496
All right, then I'll…

874
00:52:45,562 --> 00:52:47,831
I can't. I'm too tired, I can't.

875
00:52:53,604 --> 00:52:56,340
All right, my close big brother.

876
00:52:56,407 --> 00:52:59,376
Pour your little sister
another drink, please.

877
00:52:59,443 --> 00:53:01,812
Sure, have a drink, little sister.

878
00:53:10,621 --> 00:53:12,690
Um, listen. Let me ask you one thing.

879
00:53:12,756 --> 00:53:14,058
What?

880
00:53:14,124 --> 00:53:18,829
Are you and I really
just close, like brother and sister?

881
00:53:19,496 --> 00:53:21,331
You're the one who said that.

882
00:53:21,398 --> 00:53:23,233
We're just close,

883
00:53:23,300 --> 00:53:25,903
like brother and sister, you said.

884
00:53:25,969 --> 00:53:27,905
That's why I'm asking again!

885
00:53:28,505 --> 00:53:30,307
Are you and I really just close,

886
00:53:30,374 --> 00:53:33,177
nothing more than brother and sister?

887
00:53:33,243 --> 00:53:36,613
No, I don't want to be
just like brother and sister!

888
00:53:36,680 --> 00:53:38,515
-Really?
-Yes!

889
00:55:07,971 --> 00:55:09,640
Good morning.

890
00:55:09,706 --> 00:55:12,342
What brings you here so early?

891
00:55:13,911 --> 00:55:15,412
Uh, no reason.

892
00:55:15,479 --> 00:55:17,281
I was worried if Yu-na slept well.

893
00:55:26,890 --> 00:55:29,393
You're up? Why are you up so early?

894
00:55:29,459 --> 00:55:31,428
I wanted to help with breakfast.

895
00:55:33,030 --> 00:55:34,464
Um, how are you feeling?

896
00:55:34,531 --> 00:55:38,001
Oh, I feel much better after resting.

897
00:55:39,102 --> 00:55:40,704
That's a relief.

898
00:55:40,771 --> 00:55:44,675
Um… And I'm sorry
for imposing on you all this time.

899
00:55:47,578 --> 00:55:48,812
What do you mean?

900
00:55:48,879 --> 00:55:51,648
I should get going.
I can't keep imposing on you.

901
00:55:51,715 --> 00:55:53,684
Where do you think you're going?

902
00:55:53,750 --> 00:55:56,486
Don't you know reporters
are frantic to find you?

903
00:55:59,156 --> 00:56:01,692
Um, do you have somewhere to go?

904
00:56:03,827 --> 00:56:05,495
I'll have to find a place.

905
00:56:10,567 --> 00:56:14,037
If you don't have anywhere to go,
just stay here.

906
00:56:15,939 --> 00:56:17,007
What?

907
00:56:17,074 --> 00:56:19,776
I owe you a favor anyway.

908
00:56:19,843 --> 00:56:21,845
And if Min-ho's pretty friend leaves,

909
00:56:21,912 --> 00:56:24,348
he'll be really sad too.

910
00:56:24,414 --> 00:56:27,484
In return, you have to earn your keep.

911
00:56:27,551 --> 00:56:29,419
-Okay.
-Really?

912
00:56:29,486 --> 00:56:32,422
Thank you so much! Really, thank you!

913
00:56:32,489 --> 00:56:34,658
Oh, stop it.

914
00:56:35,225 --> 00:56:37,861
I'm making breakfast, so help me out.

915
00:56:41,465 --> 00:56:43,567
Why on earth are you doing this to me?

916
00:56:43,634 --> 00:56:45,002
Don't smile at everyone.

917
00:56:46,003 --> 00:56:47,704
Don't even look at other men.

918
00:56:47,771 --> 00:56:50,140
Don't talk to them or smile at them!

919
00:56:54,811 --> 00:56:57,214
Stupid alcohol is to blame, really.

920
00:56:57,281 --> 00:56:59,683
What are you muttering about so early?

921
00:56:59,750 --> 00:57:01,618
Nothing, it's nothing.

922
00:57:04,087 --> 00:57:05,389
Where are you going?

923
00:57:06,857 --> 00:57:09,459
Not that way, man!
Come here, you'll fall in!

924
00:57:10,560 --> 00:57:12,396
-Hey there, sir!
-Hello!

925
00:57:15,933 --> 00:57:17,301
No one in town is normal.

926
00:57:17,367 --> 00:57:19,403
Not a single one. Not one, really.

927
00:57:19,469 --> 00:57:21,004
I'm the only normal one.

928
00:57:21,071 --> 00:57:23,106
Oh, hey, Hwa-ran.

929
00:57:23,173 --> 00:57:24,041
Hi, sis-in-law.

930
00:57:24,107 --> 00:57:25,943
Hello, Ki-jun.

931
00:57:26,009 --> 00:57:27,444
Is your stomach okay?

932
00:57:27,511 --> 00:57:29,313
Yes, it's fine.

933
00:57:34,518 --> 00:57:37,054
Why is she smiling to herself so much?

934
00:57:39,222 --> 00:57:40,090
What's with you?

935
00:57:40,157 --> 00:57:42,659
Um, Ki-jun, please try some of this.

936
00:57:42,726 --> 00:57:44,628
It will settle your stomach fast.

937
00:57:45,295 --> 00:57:47,030
Oh, yes, thank you.

938
00:57:49,433 --> 00:57:51,234
Hwa-ran, can we talk a moment?

939
00:57:53,770 --> 00:57:55,739
Hwa-ran, what are you doing now?

940
00:57:55,806 --> 00:57:58,575
You told me not to look at others,

941
00:57:58,642 --> 00:58:01,478
and not to talk or smile at them.

942
00:58:01,545 --> 00:58:03,246
Um, about that…

943
00:58:03,313 --> 00:58:07,017
I did, but it's still way too obvious.

944
00:58:07,084 --> 00:58:09,419
And I think you have the wrong idea.

945
00:58:09,486 --> 00:58:12,489
When I told you yesterday
not to smile at other people,

946
00:58:13,123 --> 00:58:16,660
I mean, it doesn't mean I like you.

947
00:58:17,828 --> 00:58:19,896
Yes, I understand.

948
00:58:19,963 --> 00:58:21,798
I will be on my way then.

949
00:58:27,070 --> 00:58:28,238
Um, wait…

950
00:58:30,140 --> 00:58:31,541
I'm losing my mind.

951
00:58:35,012 --> 00:58:38,415
Even plastic mulch
can't stop these darn weeds.

952
00:58:38,482 --> 00:58:40,617
Ugh! They just keep poking through.

953
00:58:40,684 --> 00:58:42,819
They keep coming up. Jeez, so tough!

954
00:58:43,487 --> 00:58:45,155
By the way, I'm glad

955
00:58:45,222 --> 00:58:47,024
Yu-na can at least stay with us.

956
00:58:47,090 --> 00:58:50,394
Right, she had nowhere else to go.

957
00:58:51,328 --> 00:58:55,065
So how long are you keeping Yu-na here?

958
00:58:55,132 --> 00:58:56,400
What else can I do?

959
00:58:56,466 --> 00:58:58,135
She'd only suffer in Seoul.

960
00:58:58,201 --> 00:59:01,905
Besides, do you think
that CEO would protect Yu-na now?

961
00:59:01,972 --> 00:59:06,109
And how long do you plan
to play Yu-na's guardian like that?

962
00:59:06,877 --> 00:59:08,678
-Meaning what?
-It's just funny.

963
00:59:08,745 --> 00:59:11,314
You're in no position
to worry about Yu-na now.

964
00:59:13,650 --> 00:59:15,685
Why are you picking fights with me?

965
00:59:15,752 --> 00:59:17,487
Do you hate having Yu-na here?

966
00:59:17,554 --> 00:59:19,990
Yes, I'm not particularly thrilled.

967
00:59:20,057 --> 00:59:22,259
What's with you two again? Stop it.

968
00:59:22,325 --> 00:59:24,561
Why do you two keep doing this lately?

969
00:59:24,628 --> 00:59:26,396
Jeez, forget it. Just drop it.

970
00:59:26,463 --> 00:59:28,565
Right, drop it and just pull weeds.

971
00:59:30,367 --> 00:59:31,234
Hello.

972
00:59:31,301 --> 00:59:33,303
-Hello.
-Hello, sir.

973
00:59:33,837 --> 00:59:36,673
Right, keep up the good work.

974
00:59:36,740 --> 00:59:39,342
-Yes, take care, sir.
-Get home safely.

975
00:59:39,409 --> 00:59:41,244
-Take care.
-Okay.

976
00:59:46,883 --> 00:59:48,018
Hey! Hey!

977
00:59:48,618 --> 00:59:50,887
That guy just spoke, right? Right?

978
00:59:50,954 --> 00:59:53,023
He spoke! He actually spoke! Wow.

979
00:59:53,090 --> 00:59:54,591
Hey, what's going on here?

980
00:59:54,658 --> 00:59:56,993
What happened in this town overnight?

981
00:59:57,060 --> 00:59:58,962
It can't be.

982
01:00:00,097 --> 01:00:01,465
No way.

983
01:00:06,236 --> 01:00:07,904
Something must've happened.

984
01:00:07,971 --> 01:00:12,375
Seriously, nobody in this town
is normal. Not one normal person.

985
01:00:21,051 --> 01:00:22,552
I said I'm going alone.

986
01:00:22,619 --> 01:00:24,221
Why sit around doing nothing?

987
01:00:24,287 --> 01:00:27,124
Plus, if the two of us dig together,

988
01:00:27,190 --> 01:00:29,092
our odds will be much higher.

989
01:00:30,760 --> 01:00:33,130
Fine, whatever. Just follow my lead.

990
01:00:33,196 --> 01:00:35,232
Got it? Let's go.

991
01:00:35,732 --> 01:00:37,634
Got it.

992
01:00:41,905 --> 01:00:45,675
What on earth is going on
between Su-yeon and that woman?

993
01:00:45,742 --> 01:00:47,544
Don't tell me they're in love…

994
01:00:47,611 --> 01:00:49,646
No, no, that can't be.

995
01:00:49,713 --> 01:00:51,681
That makes no sense! No sense at all!

996
01:00:53,750 --> 01:00:56,620
What's that about being
too conservative to understand?

997
01:00:56,686 --> 01:00:59,356
And why were they
hugging each other, seriously?

998
01:00:59,422 --> 01:01:01,391
I don't get it. I just don't get it.

999
01:01:06,163 --> 01:01:08,899
It's cold, so cold.
Why is it this cold, really?

1000
01:01:11,001 --> 01:01:12,869
It's so cold, so cold.

1001
01:01:14,838 --> 01:01:17,340
Come on, hurry up! Quit dawdling!

1002
01:01:17,407 --> 01:01:20,544
All right, girl. It's freezing!

1003
01:01:20,610 --> 01:01:23,980
Right, I forgot my mask. Ta-da!

1004
01:01:24,047 --> 01:01:28,285
I got it at the market earlier.
What do you think? Killer, right?

1005
01:01:28,952 --> 01:01:30,287
Killer, my foot.

1006
01:01:30,353 --> 01:01:32,189
Put it on fast, then! No time.

1007
01:01:32,255 --> 01:01:34,324
Don't you be jealous now!

1008
01:01:39,396 --> 01:01:41,631
They're too far away. I can't see.

1009
01:01:42,732 --> 01:01:44,734
I can't even hear them, darn it.

1010
01:01:44,801 --> 01:01:47,737
Here comes the champion of justice!

1011
01:01:48,305 --> 01:01:49,873
Killer, right?

1012
01:01:55,378 --> 01:01:56,780
What is this?

1013
01:01:57,380 --> 01:02:00,250
I told you we have no time, seriously!

1014
01:02:00,317 --> 01:02:02,719
Su-yeon, pull this off for me.

1015
01:02:02,786 --> 01:02:05,088
What is it this time?

1016
01:02:09,025 --> 01:02:12,696
This thing keeps getting in my mouth!

1017
01:02:12,762 --> 01:02:14,331
Just pull this thing off.

1018
01:02:17,267 --> 01:02:18,902
It won't budge, this thing.

1019
01:02:20,270 --> 01:02:21,771
Do something about it!

1020
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:24,541
All right, fine.

1021
01:02:26,643 --> 01:02:28,745
The thread won't budge. Just rip it?

1022
01:02:28,812 --> 01:02:29,679
Got a knife?

1023
01:02:29,746 --> 01:02:32,649
-I don't.
-You don't even have a knife?

1024
01:02:33,750 --> 01:02:35,719
Come here.

1025
01:02:41,291 --> 01:02:42,192
What… is that?

1026
01:02:46,930 --> 01:02:48,932
Damn that hag who sold me this!

1027
01:02:48,999 --> 01:02:50,066
I'll go tomorrow

1028
01:02:50,133 --> 01:02:52,035
and tear her apart on the spot!

1029
01:03:00,577 --> 01:03:02,245
Slow down for me!

1030
01:03:17,260 --> 01:03:18,695
Hyeok.

1031
01:03:19,529 --> 01:03:20,397
Why out here?

1032
01:03:22,932 --> 01:03:26,102
Couldn't sleep. Thought I'd stargaze.

1033
01:03:29,539 --> 01:03:31,508
I guess you're not even worried.

1034
01:03:31,574 --> 01:03:34,210
You fought fiercely to reach the top.

1035
01:03:35,845 --> 01:03:39,749
So how long will you keep
leaning on Min-gi like that?

1036
01:03:40,583 --> 01:03:42,352
Isn't that going a bit too far?

1037
01:03:43,253 --> 01:03:45,588
If it were me, I couldn't do that.

1038
01:03:47,123 --> 01:03:49,826
-I'm sorry.
-Go back to Seoul.

1039
01:03:50,360 --> 01:03:53,596
Don't stay here and wear everyone out.

1040
01:03:53,663 --> 01:03:55,732
What nonsense are you spouting now?

1041
01:03:58,101 --> 01:03:59,002
Min-gi.

1042
01:04:00,704 --> 01:04:02,505
Who are you to tell Yu-na to go?

1043
01:04:06,076 --> 01:04:07,177
Enter her guardian.

1044
01:04:07,243 --> 01:04:09,779
You bastard, you always run your mouth!

1045
01:04:09,846 --> 01:04:10,947
Say that again!

1046
01:04:11,014 --> 01:04:13,249
What? Her guardian? Guardian?

1047
01:04:14,250 --> 01:04:16,353
-Let go of me!
-Oh, look at you.

1048
01:04:16,419 --> 01:04:18,121
I'm about to get angry now.

1049
01:04:18,188 --> 01:04:20,223
-Oh, do get angry!
-Why is it so loud?

1050
01:04:20,290 --> 01:04:22,225
Get angry! Hey, get angry! Do it!

1051
01:04:22,292 --> 01:04:23,893
What are you two doing?

1052
01:04:24,561 --> 01:04:25,762
Talk! I said talk!

1053
01:04:25,829 --> 01:04:27,263
Hey! What are you doing?

1054
01:04:27,330 --> 01:04:28,765
Get angry! Come on!

